{"timestamp":"2026-09-06T21:45:27.117Z","ordinal":8772,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a07177-9855-71a2-89cd-4a9a37cdbfcb","turn_id":"01a078ac-bf7f-7050-adcc-4d223220149d","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-eb8eb05d-e4b0-4160-b5f4-da448f5babde","process_id":"62076","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","gh api graphql -f query='query { repository(owner:\"jdx\",name:\"mise\") { pullRequest(number:12865) { reviewThreads(last:100) { nodes { id isResolved comments(first:1) { nodes { databaseId body } } } } } } }' --jq '.data.repository.pullRequest.reviewThreads.nodes[]|select(.isResolved|not)|{pr:12865,id,comment:.comments.nodes[0].databaseId,body:(.comments.nodes[0].body|gsub(\"<details>[\\\\s\\\\S]*?</details>\";\"\")|split(\"<!--\")[0]|.[0:1200])}'"],"cwd":"file:///Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/141d/mise","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"gh api graphql -f query='query { repository(owner:\"jdx\",name:\"mise\") { pullRequest(number:12865) { reviewThreads(last:100) { nodes { id isResolved comments(first:1) { nodes { databaseId body } } } } } } }' --jq '.data.repository.pullRequest.reviewThreads.nodes[]|select(.isResolved|not)|{pr:12865,id,comment:.comments.nodes[0].databaseId,body:(.comments.nodes[0].body|gsub(\"<details>[\\\\s\\\\S]*?</details>\";\"\")|split(\"<!--\")[0]|.[0:1200])}'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"{\"body\":\"_🎯 Functional Correctness_ | _🟡 Minor_ | _⚡ Quick win_\\n\\n**Record the start of the current sync-failure streak.** When `sync()` fails before any fetch or publish succeeds, it persists `last_error` but no failure timestamp. `doctor` therefore keeps printing `last sync error (transient)` for a permanently unreachable origin. Persist the first-failure timestamp for the current streak, preserve it across later failures, clear it after success, and use it to calculate `failing_for`.\\n\\n\\n\\n\",\"comment\":3944671871,\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fthu_\",\"pr\":12865}\n{\"body\":\"_🔒 Security \\u0026 Privacy_ | _🟡 Minor_ | _⚡ Quick win_\\n\\n\\n\\n\",\"comment\":3944671879,\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fthvD\",\"pr\":12865}\n{\"body\":\"### Checkpoint re-upload can brick sync\\n\\n**High Severity**\\n\\n\",\"comment\":3944672288,\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fthzJ\",\"pr\":12865}\n{\"body\":\"_🔒 Security \\u0026 Privacy_ | _🟠 Major_ | _⚡ Quick win_\\n\\n\\n\\n\",\"comment\":3944731614,\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6ftrhH\",\"pr\":12865}\n{\"body\":\"_🔒 Security \\u0026 Privacy_ | _🟠 Major_ | _🏗️ Heavy lift_\\n\\n\\n\\n\",\"comment\":3944731660,\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6ftrhs\",\"pr\":12865}\n{\"body\":\"### This-machine refs use backups\\n\\n**Medium Severity**\\n\\n\",\"comment\":3945289138,\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fvFtn\",\"pr\":12865}\n{\"body\":\"_🗄️ Data Integrity \\u0026 Integration_ | _🟠 Major_ | _⚡ Quick win_\\n\\n\\n\\n**Reject unknown keys in incoming whole-file declarations.**\\n\\nWhen a table contains a valid key such as `source`, `file_entry_from_toml` accepts it. `FileTomlEntry` then discards an unknown key such as `shrae = false`. `merge_file_entry` applies the default `share = true`, so synchronization can publish the file against the declaration intent.\\n\\nValidate the original table keys in `validate_incoming_files`, or use an incoming-only strict deserializer. Add a regression test for a valid declaration with an unknown policy key.\\n\\n\\n\\n\",\"comment\":3945310318,\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fvJLQ\",\"pr\":12865}\n{\"body\":\"_🗄️ Data Integrity \\u0026 Integration_ | _🟡 Minor_ | _⚡ Quick win_\\n\\n**A variant name that contains `/` maps back to the wrong local path.**\\n\\n`unchecked_branch_path` inserts `variant` into the stream segment without restricting it. `is_safe_branch_path` splits on `/`, so a variant such as `a/b` passes and produces `tracked/home@a/b/.zshrc`. `locate` strips `tracked/home@` and splits `rest` at the first `/`, so it returns `variant: \\\"a\\\"` and `path: $HOME/b/.zshrc`. The round trip is not stable, and a pull writes the file to a different local path than the one that published it.\\n\\nReject a variant that contains `/` (and, for symmetry with the stream separator, `@`) when the branch path is built. The existing test covers `bad:variant` but not `a/b`.\\n\\n\\n\\n\",\"comment\":3945310321,\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fvJLR\",\"pr\":12865}\n{\"body\":\"_🔒 Security \\u0026 Privacy_ | _🟠 Major_ | _⚡ Quick win_\\n\\n\\n\\n\",\"comment\":3945310329,\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fvJLV\",\"pr\":12865}\n{\"body\":\"_🗄️ Data Integrity \\u0026 Integration_ | _🟡 Minor_ | _⚡ Quick win_\\n\\n**Take the sync lock before you rewrite `sync.json`.**\\n\\n`bootstrap_completed` performs a read-modify-write of the whole `SyncStatus` file without holding the lock that `sync` and `pull` take at Line 366. If a sync is in progress, `write_status` here replaces the file with a snapshot read before the sync finished. That discards fields the sync just recorded, such as `uploaded`, `conflicts`, `pending_applications`, and `upload_since`, and the discarded `uploaded` set causes checkpoints to be uploaded again.\\n\\nAcquire the same `sync.lock` around the read and the write. `lock` needs a `Store`, so either accept one here or extract a lock helper that takes a state directory.\\n\\n\\n\\n\",\"comment\":3945310331,\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fvJLX\",\"pr\":12865}\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"{\"body\":\"_🎯 Functional Correctness_ | _🟡 Minor_ | _⚡ Quick win_\\n\\n**Record the start of the current sync-failure streak.** When `sync()` fails before any fetch or publish succeeds, it persists `last_error` but no failure timestamp. `doctor` therefore keeps printing `last sync error (transient)` for a permanently unreachable origin. Persist the first-failure timestamp for the current streak, preserve it across later failures, clear it after success, and use it to calculate `failing_for`.\\n\\n\\n\\n\",\"comment\":3944671871,\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fthu_\",\"pr\":12865}\n{\"body\":\"_🔒 Security \\u0026 Privacy_ | _🟡 Minor_ | _⚡ Quick win_\\n\\n\\n\\n\",\"comment\":3944671879,\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fthvD\",\"pr\":12865}\n{\"body\":\"### Checkpoint re-upload can brick sync\\n\\n**High Severity**\\n\\n\",\"comment\":3944672288,\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fthzJ\",\"pr\":12865}\n{\"body\":\"_🔒 Security \\u0026 Privacy_ | _🟠 Major_ | _⚡ Quick win_\\n\\n\\n\\n\",\"comment\":3944731614,\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6ftrhH\",\"pr\":12865}\n{\"body\":\"_🔒 Security \\u0026 Privacy_ | _🟠 Major_ | _🏗️ Heavy lift_\\n\\n\\n\\n\",\"comment\":3944731660,\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6ftrhs\",\"pr\":12865}\n{\"body\":\"### This-machine refs use backups\\n\\n**Medium Severity**\\n\\n\",\"comment\":3945289138,\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fvFtn\",\"pr\":12865}\n{\"body\":\"_🗄️ Data Integrity \\u0026 Integration_ | _🟠 Major_ | _⚡ Quick win_\\n\\n\\n\\n**Reject unknown keys in incoming whole-file declarations.**\\n\\nWhen a table contains a valid key such as `source`, `file_entry_from_toml` accepts it. `FileTomlEntry` then discards an unknown key such as `shrae = false`. `merge_file_entry` applies the default `share = true`, so synchronization can publish the file against the declaration intent.\\n\\nValidate the original table keys in `validate_incoming_files`, or use an incoming-only strict deserializer. Add a regression test for a valid declaration with an unknown policy key.\\n\\n\\n\\n\",\"comment\":3945310318,\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fvJLQ\",\"pr\":12865}\n{\"body\":\"_🗄️ Data Integrity \\u0026 Integration_ | _🟡 Minor_ | _⚡ Quick win_\\n\\n**A variant name that contains `/` maps back to the wrong local path.**\\n\\n`unchecked_branch_path` inserts `variant` into the stream segment without restricting it. `is_safe_branch_path` splits on `/`, so a variant such as `a/b` passes and produces `tracked/home@a/b/.zshrc`. `locate` strips `tracked/home@` and splits `rest` at the first `/`, so it returns `variant: \\\"a\\\"` and `path: $HOME/b/.zshrc`. The round trip is not stable, and a pull writes the file to a different local path than the one that published it.\\n\\nReject a variant that contains `/` (and, for symmetry with the stream separator, `@`) when the branch path is built. The existing test covers `bad:variant` but not `a/b`.\\n\\n\\n\\n\",\"comment\":3945310321,\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fvJLR\",\"pr\":12865}\n{\"body\":\"_🔒 Security \\u0026 Privacy_ | _🟠 Major_ | _⚡ Quick win_\\n\\n\\n\\n\",\"comment\":3945310329,\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fvJLV\",\"pr\":12865}\n{\"body\":\"_🗄️ Data Integrity \\u0026 Integration_ | _🟡 Minor_ | _⚡ Quick win_\\n\\n**Take the sync lock before you rewrite `sync.json`.**\\n\\n`bootstrap_completed` performs a read-modify-write of the whole `SyncStatus` file without holding the lock that `sync` and `pull` take at Line 366. If a sync is in progress, `write_status` here replaces the file with a snapshot read before the sync finished. That discards fields the sync just recorded, such as `uploaded`, `conflicts`, `pending_applications`, and `upload_since`, and the discarded `uploaded` set causes checkpoints to be uploaded again.\\n\\nAcquire the same `sync.lock` around the read and the write. `lock` needs a `Store`, so either accept one here or extract a lock helper that takes a state directory.\\n\\n\\n\\n\",\"comment\":3945310331,\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fvJLX\",\"pr\":12865}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":638531541},"formatted_output":"{\"body\":\"_🎯 Functional Correctness_ | _🟡 Minor_ | _⚡ Quick win_\\n\\n**Record the start of the current sync-failure streak.** When `sync()` fails before any fetch or publish succeeds, it persists `last_error` but no failure timestamp. `doctor` therefore keeps printing `last sync error (transient)` for a permanently unreachable origin. Persist the first-failure timestamp for the current streak, preserve it across later failures, clear it after success, and use it to calculate `failing_for`.\\n\\n\\n\\n\",\"comment\":3944671871,\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fthu_\",\"pr\":12865}\n{\"body\":\"_🔒 Security \\u0026 Privacy_ | _🟡 Minor_ | _⚡ Quick win_\\n\\n\\n\\n\",\"comment\":3944671879,\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fthvD\",\"pr\":12865}\n{\"body\":\"### Checkpoint re-upload can brick sync\\n\\n**High Severity**\\n\\n\",\"comment\":3944672288,\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fthzJ\",\"pr\":12865}\n{\"body\":\"_🔒 Security \\u0026 Privacy_ | _🟠 Major_ | _⚡ Quick win_\\n\\n\\n\\n\",\"comment\":3944731614,\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6ftrhH\",\"pr\":12865}\n{\"body\":\"_🔒 Security \\u0026 Privacy_ | _🟠 Major_ | _🏗️ Heavy lift_\\n\\n\\n\\n\",\"comment\":3944731660,\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6ftrhs\",\"pr\":12865}\n{\"body\":\"### This-machine refs use backups\\n\\n**Medium Severity**\\n\\n\",\"comment\":3945289138,\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fvFtn\",\"pr\":12865}\n{\"body\":\"_🗄️ Data Integrity \\u0026 Integration_ | _🟠 Major_ | _⚡ Quick win_\\n\\n\\n\\n**Reject unknown keys in incoming whole-file declarations.**\\n\\nWhen a table contains a valid key such as `source`, `file_entry_from_toml` accepts it. `FileTomlEntry` then discards an unknown key such as `shrae = false`. `merge_file_entry` applies the default `share = true`, so synchronization can publish the file against the declaration intent.\\n\\nValidate the original table keys in `validate_incoming_files`, or use an incoming-only strict deserializer. Add a regression test for a valid declaration with an unknown policy key.\\n\\n\\n\\n\",\"comment\":3945310318,\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fvJLQ\",\"pr\":12865}\n{\"body\":\"_🗄️ Data Integrity \\u0026 Integration_ | _🟡 Minor_ | _⚡ Quick win_\\n\\n**A variant name that contains `/` maps back to the wrong local path.**\\n\\n`unchecked_branch_path` inserts `variant` into the stream segment without restricting it. `is_safe_branch_path` splits on `/`, so a variant such as `a/b` passes and produces `tracked/home@a/b/.zshrc`. `locate` strips `tracked/home@` and splits `rest` at the first `/`, so it returns `variant: \\\"a\\\"` and `path: $HOME/b/.zshrc`. The round trip is not stable, and a pull writes the file to a different local path than the one that published it.\\n\\nReject a variant that contains `/` (and, for symmetry with the stream separator, `@`) when the branch path is built. The existing test covers `bad:variant` but not `a/b`.\\n\\n\\n\\n\",\"comment\":3945310321,\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fvJLR\",\"pr\":12865}\n{\"body\":\"_🔒 Security \\u0026 Privacy_ | _🟠 Major_ | _⚡ Quick win_\\n\\n\\n\\n\",\"comment\":3945310329,\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fvJLV\",\"pr\":12865}\n{\"body\":\"_🗄️ Data Integrity \\u0026 Integration_ | _🟡 Minor_ | _⚡ Quick win_\\n\\n**Take the sync lock before you rewrite `sync.json`.**\\n\\n`bootstrap_completed` performs a read-modify-write of the whole `SyncStatus` file without holding the lock that `sync` and `pull` take at Line 366. If a sync is in progress, `write_status` here replaces the file with a snapshot read before the sync finished. That discards fields the sync just recorded, such as `uploaded`, `conflicts`, `pending_applications`, and `upload_since`, and the discarded `uploaded` set causes checkpoints to be uploaded again.\\n\\nAcquire the same `sync.lock` around the read and the write. `lock` needs a `Store`, so either accept one here or extract a lock helper that takes a state directory.\\n\\n\\n\\n\",\"comment\":3945310331,\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fvJLX\",\"pr\":12865}\n"},"started_at_ms":1788731126478,"completed_at_ms":1788731127117}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-06T21:45:27.722Z","ordinal":8773,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a07177-9855-71a2-89cd-4a9a37cdbfcb","turn_id":"01a078ac-bf7f-7050-adcc-4d223220149d","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-296217b3-eadc-4c70-93de-91c3ff3395f3","process_id":"68546","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","gh api graphql -f query='query { repository(owner:\"jdx\",name:\"mise\") { pullRequest(number:12882) { reviewThreads(last:100) { nodes { id isResolved comments(first:1) { nodes { databaseId body } } } } } } }' --jq '.data.repository.pullRequest.reviewThreads.nodes[]|select(.isResolved|not)|{pr:12882,id,comment:.comments.nodes[0].databaseId,body:(.comments.nodes[0].body|gsub(\"<details>[\\\\s\\\\S]*?</details>\";\"\")|split(\"<!--\")[0]|.[0:1200])}'"],"cwd":"file:///Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/141d/mise","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"gh api graphql -f query='query { repository(owner:\"jdx\",name:\"mise\") { pullRequest(number:12882) { reviewThreads(last:100) { nodes { id isResolved comments(first:1) { nodes { databaseId body } } } } } } }' --jq '.data.repository.pullRequest.reviewThreads.nodes[]|select(.isResolved|not)|{pr:12882,id,comment:.comments.nodes[0].databaseId,body:(.comments.nodes[0].body|gsub(\"<details>[\\\\s\\\\S]*?</details>\";\"\")|split(\"<!--\")[0]|.[0:1200])}'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"{\"body\":\"_🎯 Functional Correctness_ | _🟠 Major_ | _⚡ Quick win_\\n\\n**Remove the stale origin-local sync override.** `Settings::get()` loads `settings.history.sync` from `config.local.toml`, while `mise settings set history.sync ...` writes only the global file. Therefore, `--sync fetch-only` can keep the effective mode at `fetch-only` after the global mode changes. Comparing against a global-only value is not sufficient because `write_config(..., None)` currently leaves the existing local key. Remove that key when the global mode should control sync, without changing the `onboard.rs` path that uses `None` to preserve settings.\\n\\n\\n\\n\",\"comment\":3944697691,\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6ftl4k\",\"pr\":12882}\n{\"body\":\"_🎯 Functional Correctness_ | _🟠 Major_ | _🏗️ Heavy lift_\\n\\n**Keep the normal bootstrap preview in the target-side dry-run path.**\\n\\nWhen the target has history synchronization enabled, `run_from()` returns immediately after `onboard::from_git` when `self.dry_run` is true. It returns before `run_child_bootstrap(config_dir)`. Therefore, this fetch-and-transfer path previews repository synchronization only. It does not preview the ordinary bootstrap resources that a real run applies.\\n\\nPreserve the no-persistence behavior, but run an equivalent target-side bootstrap plan against the fetched configuration. Add an end-to-end assertion for at least one bootstrap resource.\\n\\n\\n\\n\",\"comment\":3944932227,\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fuMZC\",\"pr\":12882}\n{\"body\":\"### Purge fails to disconnect after delete\\n\\n**High Severity**\\n\\n\",\"comment\":3945294364,\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fvGkw\",\"pr\":12882}\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"{\"body\":\"_🎯 Functional Correctness_ | _🟠 Major_ | _⚡ Quick win_\\n\\n**Remove the stale origin-local sync override.** `Settings::get()` loads `settings.history.sync` from `config.local.toml`, while `mise settings set history.sync ...` writes only the global file. Therefore, `--sync fetch-only` can keep the effective mode at `fetch-only` after the global mode changes. Comparing against a global-only value is not sufficient because `write_config(..., None)` currently leaves the existing local key. Remove that key when the global mode should control sync, without changing the `onboard.rs` path that uses `None` to preserve settings.\\n\\n\\n\\n\",\"comment\":3944697691,\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6ftl4k\",\"pr\":12882}\n{\"body\":\"_🎯 Functional Correctness_ | _🟠 Major_ | _🏗️ Heavy lift_\\n\\n**Keep the normal bootstrap preview in the target-side dry-run path.**\\n\\nWhen the target has history synchronization enabled, `run_from()` returns immediately after `onboard::from_git` when `self.dry_run` is true. It returns before `run_child_bootstrap(config_dir)`. Therefore, this fetch-and-transfer path previews repository synchronization only. It does not preview the ordinary bootstrap resources that a real run applies.\\n\\nPreserve the no-persistence behavior, but run an equivalent target-side bootstrap plan against the fetched configuration. Add an end-to-end assertion for at least one bootstrap resource.\\n\\n\\n\\n\",\"comment\":3944932227,\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fuMZC\",\"pr\":12882}\n{\"body\":\"### Purge fails to disconnect after delete\\n\\n**High Severity**\\n\\n\",\"comment\":3945294364,\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fvGkw\",\"pr\":12882}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":407445375},"formatted_output":"{\"body\":\"_🎯 Functional Correctness_ | _🟠 Major_ | _⚡ Quick win_\\n\\n**Remove the stale origin-local sync override.** `Settings::get()` loads `settings.history.sync` from `config.local.toml`, while `mise settings set history.sync ...` writes only the global file. Therefore, `--sync fetch-only` can keep the effective mode at `fetch-only` after the global mode changes. Comparing against a global-only value is not sufficient because `write_config(..., None)` currently leaves the existing local key. Remove that key when the global mode should control sync, without changing the `onboard.rs` path that uses `None` to preserve settings.\\n\\n\\n\\n\",\"comment\":3944697691,\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6ftl4k\",\"pr\":12882}\n{\"body\":\"_🎯 Functional Correctness_ | _🟠 Major_ | _🏗️ Heavy lift_\\n\\n**Keep the normal bootstrap preview in the target-side dry-run path.**\\n\\nWhen the target has history synchronization enabled, `run_from()` returns immediately after `onboard::from_git` when `self.dry_run` is true. It returns before `run_child_bootstrap(config_dir)`. Therefore, this fetch-and-transfer path previews repository synchronization only. It does not preview the ordinary bootstrap resources that a real run applies.\\n\\nPreserve the no-persistence behavior, but run an equivalent target-side bootstrap plan against the fetched configuration. Add an end-to-end assertion for at least one bootstrap resource.\\n\\n\\n\\n\",\"comment\":3944932227,\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fuMZC\",\"pr\":12882}\n{\"body\":\"### Purge fails to disconnect after delete\\n\\n**High Severity**\\n\\n\",\"comment\":3945294364,\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fvGkw\",\"pr\":12882}\n"},"started_at_ms":1788731127315,"completed_at_ms":1788731127722}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-06T21:45:27.756Z","ordinal":8774,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a078ae-f7cc-7122-871b-96c427f552cc","call_id":"call_8qw15NYJ3YtTMhtPGWafKlqU","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 4.5 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"7bc843\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.478794583,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":0,\"output\":\"\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"e3a5fa\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.555784583,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":331,\"output\":\"{\\\"body\\\":\\\"\\\\u003ca href=\\\\\\\"#\\\\\\\"\\\\u003e\\\\u003cimg alt=\\\\\\\"P1\\\\\\\" src=\\\\\\\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p1.svg?v=9\\\\\\\" align=\\\\\\\"top\\\\\\\"\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e **Unreadable Directory Aborts Rollback**\\\\n\\\\nIf an otherwise disposable directory contains an unreadable descendant, this scan propagates the traversal error and aborts the entire rollback or undo. The normal history walker records unreadable paths as omitted and continues, while this scan only decides whether an optional directory-cleanup step is safe. An inspection failure should therefore preserve the directory instead of preventing unrelated planned changes from being restored.\\\\n\\\\n\\\\u003ca href=\\\\\\\"https://app.greptile.com/ide/claude-code?prompt=This%20is%20a%20comment%20left%20during%20a%20code%20review.%0APath%3A%20src%2Fsystem%2Fhistory%2Freplay.rs%0ALine%3A%201010-1011%0A%0AComment%3A%0A**Unreadable%20Directory%20Aborts%20Rollback**%0A%0AIf%20an%20otherwise%20disposable%20directory%20contains%20an%20unreadable%20descendant%2C%20this%20scan%20propagates%20the%20traversal%20error%20and%20aborts%20the%20entire%20rollback%20or%20undo.%20The%20normal%20history%20walker%20records%20unreadable%20paths%20as%20omitted%20and%20continues%2C%20while%20this%20scan%20only%20decides%20whet\\\",\\\"comment\\\":3945285524,\\\"id\\\":\\\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fvFHf\\\",\\\"pr\\\":12835}\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"60a768\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.504019834,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":0,\"output\":\"\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"fb681f\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.707988458,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":0,\"output\":\"\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"6bf891\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.638535125,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":954,\"output\":\"{\\\"body\\\":\\\"_🎯 Functional Correctness_ | _🟡 Minor_ | _⚡ Quick win_\\\\n\\\\n**Record the start of the current sync-failure streak.** When `sync()` fails before any fetch or publish succeeds, it persists `last_error` but no failure timestamp. `doctor` therefore keeps printing `last sync error (transient)` for a permanently unreachable origin. Persist the first-failure timestamp for the current streak, preserve it across later failures, clear it after success, and use it to calculate `failing_for`.\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n\\\",\\\"comment\\\":3944671871,\\\"id\\\":\\\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fthu_\\\",\\\"pr\\\":12865}\\n{\\\"body\\\":\\\"_🔒 Security \\\\u0026 Privacy_ | _🟡 Minor_ | _⚡ Quick win_\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n\\\",\\\"comment\\\":3944671879,\\\"id\\\":\\\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fthvD\\\",\\\"pr\\\":12865}\\n{\\\"body\\\":\\\"### Checkpoint re-upload can brick sync\\\\n\\\\n**High Severity**\\\\n\\\\n\\\",\\\"comment\\\":3944672288,\\\"id\\\":\\\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fthzJ\\\",\\\"pr\\\":12865}\\n{\\\"body\\\":\\\"_🔒 Security \\\\u0026 Privacy_ | _🟠 Major_ | _⚡ Quick win_\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n\\\",\\\"comment\\\":3944731614,\\\"id\\\":\\\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6ftrhH\\\",\\\"pr\\\":12865}\\n{\\\"body\\\":\\\"_🔒 Security \\\\u0026 Privacy_ | _🟠 Major_ | _🏗️ Heavy lift_\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n\\\",\\\"comment\\\":3944731660,\\\"id\\\":\\\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6ftrhs\\\",\\\"pr\\\":12865}\\n{\\\"body\\\":\\\"### This-machine refs use backups\\\\n\\\\n**Medium Severity**\\\\n\\\\n\\\",\\\"comment\\\":3945289138,\\\"id\\\":\\\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fvFtn\\\",\\\"pr\\\":12865}\\n{\\\"body\\\":\\\"_🗄️ Data Integrity \\\\u0026 Integration_ | _🟠 Major_ | _⚡ Quick win_\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n**Reject unknown keys in incoming whole-file declarations.**\\\\n\\\\nWhen a table contains a valid key such as `source`, `file_entry_from_toml` accepts it. `FileTomlEntry` then discards an unknown key such as `shrae = false`. `merge_file_entry` applies the default `share = true`, so synchronization can publish the file against the declaration intent.\\\\n\\\\nValidate the original table keys in `validate_incoming_files`, or use an incoming-only strict deserializer. Add a regression test for a valid declaration with an unknown policy key.\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n\\\",\\\"comment\\\":3945310318,\\\"id\\\":\\\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fvJLQ\\\",\\\"pr\\\":12865}\\n{\\\"body\\\":\\\"_🗄️ Data Integrity \\\\u0026 Integration_ | _🟡 Minor_ | _⚡ Quick win_\\\\n\\\\n**A variant name that contains `/` maps back to the wrong local path.**\\\\n\\\\n`unchecked_branch_path` inserts `variant` into the stream segment without restricting it. `is_safe_branch_path` splits on `/`, so a variant such as `a/b` passes and produces `tracked/home@a/b/.zshrc`. `locate` strips `tracked/home@` and splits `rest` at the first `/`, so it returns `variant: \\\\\\\"a\\\\\\\"` and `path: $HOME/b/.zshrc`. The round trip is not stable, and a pull writes the file to a different local path than the one that published it.\\\\n\\\\nReject a variant that contains `/` (and, for symmetry with the stream separator, `@`) when the branch path is built. The existing test covers `bad:variant` but not `a/b`.\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n\\\",\\\"comment\\\":3945310321,\\\"id\\\":\\\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fvJLR\\\",\\\"pr\\\":12865}\\n{\\\"body\\\":\\\"_🔒 Security \\\\u0026 Privacy_ | _🟠 Major_ | _⚡ Quick win_\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n\\\",\\\"comment\\\":3945310329,\\\"id\\\":\\\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fvJLV\\\",\\\"pr\\\":12865}\\n{\\\"body\\\":\\\"_🗄️ Data Integrity \\\\u0026 Integration_ | _🟡 Minor_ | _⚡ Quick win_\\\\n\\\\n**Take the sync lock before you rewrite `sync.json`.**\\\\n\\\\n`bootstrap_completed` performs a read-modify-write of the whole `SyncStatus` file without holding the lock that `sync` and `pull` take at Line 366. If a sync is in progress, `write_status` here replaces the file with a snapshot read before the sync finished. That discards fields the sync just recorded, such as `uploaded`, `conflicts`, `pending_applications`, and `upload_since`, and the discarded `uploaded` set causes checkpoints to be uploaded again.\\\\n\\\\nAcquire the same `sync.lock` around the read and the write. `lock` needs a `Store`, so either accept one here or extract a lock helper that takes a state directory.\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n\\\",\\\"comment\\\":3945310331,\\\"id\\\":\\\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fvJLX\\\",\\\"pr\\\":12865}\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"dfe5c3\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.407457833,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":406,\"output\":\"{\\\"body\\\":\\\"_🎯 Functional Correctness_ | _🟠 Major_ | _⚡ Quick win_\\\\n\\\\n**Remove the stale origin-local sync override.** `Settings::get()` loads `settings.history.sync` from `config.local.toml`, while `mise settings set history.sync ...` writes only the global file. Therefore, `--sync fetch-only` can keep the effective mode at `fetch-only` after the global mode changes. Comparing against a global-only value is not sufficient because `write_config(..., None)` currently leaves the existing local key. Remove that key when the global mode should control sync, without changing the `onboard.rs` path that uses `None` to preserve settings.\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n\\\",\\\"comment\\\":3944697691,\\\"id\\\":\\\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6ftl4k\\\",\\\"pr\\\":12882}\\n{\\\"body\\\":\\\"_🎯 Functional Correctness_ | _🟠 Major_ | _🏗️ Heavy lift_\\\\n\\\\n**Keep the normal bootstrap preview in the target-side dry-run path.**\\\\n\\\\nWhen the target has history synchronization enabled, `run_from()` returns immediately after `onboard::from_git` when `self.dry_run` is true. It returns before `run_child_bootstrap(config_dir)`. Therefore, this fetch-and-transfer path previews repository synchronization only. It does not preview the ordinary bootstrap resources that a real run applies.\\\\n\\\\nPreserve the no-persistence behavior, but run an equivalent target-side bootstrap plan against the fetched configuration. Add an end-to-end assertion for at least one bootstrap resource.\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n\\\",\\\"comment\\\":3944932227,\\\"id\\\":\\\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fuMZC\\\",\\\"pr\\\":12882}\\n{\\\"body\\\":\\\"### Purge fails to disconnect after delete\\\\n\\\\n**High Severity**\\\\n\\\\n\\\",\\\"comment\\\":3945294364,\\\"id\\\":\\\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fvGkw\\\",\\\"pr\\\":12882}\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a078ac-bf7f-7050-adcc-4d223220149d","create_time":1788731127.756127}}}
