d file contents with the public recipients in\n+ `[history.encryption]`. These files never enter plaintext remote backups.\n++>>>>>>> 8cefe6ce9 (feat(dotfiles): encrypt shared files and support hardware identities)\n  \n  `*.local.toml` files are private by default (`share = false`) wherever they\n  are found, and credential stores under the config directory\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":5042},"formatted_output":"diff --cc docs/history.md\nindex 4e3aa3751,7a068bd02..000000000\n--- a/docs/history.md\n+++ b/docs/history.md\n@@@ -504,7 -488,8 +503,12 @@@ Each entry carries policies, set on th\n  | `share`    | Publish the saved version to the shared setup (default `true`)        |\n  | `backup`   | Include the file in remote backups (default `true` for tracked files) |\n  \n++<<<<<<< HEAD\n +Sharing and recovery backups follow these policies when you connect an origin.\n++=======\n+ Use `encrypt = true` to protect shared file contents with the public recipients in\n+ `[history.encryption]`. These files never enter plaintext remote backups.\n++>>>>>>> 8cefe6ce9 (feat(dotfiles): encrypt shared files and support hardware identities)\n  \n  `*.local.toml` files are private by default (`share = false`) wherever they\n  are found, and credential stores under the config directory\n"},"started_at_ms":1788732430065,"completed_at_ms":1788732430065}}
