{"timestamp":"2026-09-06T22:09:11.448Z","ordinal":9473,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a078c4-b118-7d90-9083-8d44b617182e","call_id":"call_qeydVVL5CmrhAZpVrN9slEf7","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 5.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"29c3d8\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000002167,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":757,\"output\":\"docs/history.md:4:> Dotfile tracking and history are experimental. Enable them with\\ndocs/history.md:5:> `mise settings experimental=true`. Interfaces and storage formats may change.\\ndocs/history.md:348:and `[history.encryption].recipients`. The `[env]` age directives remain experimental.\\ne2e/cli/test_dotfiles_sync_encrypted:6:# generated. Runs with experimental settings disabled.\\ne2e/cli/test_dotfiles_sync_encrypted:11:export MISE_EXPERIMENTAL=0\\ne2e/cli/test_dotfiles_sync_encrypted:31:  MISE_CACHE_DIR=\\\"$2/.cache/mise\\\" MISE_TRUSTED_CONFIG_PATHS=\\\"$2\\\" MISE_EXPERIMENTAL=0\\ne2e/cli/test_dotfiles_sync_encrypted:56:assert_fail \\\"mise set --age-encrypt X=1 --age-recipient $PUB 2>&1\\\" \\\"experimental\\\"\\ne2e/cli/test_dotfiles_sync_encrypted:72:assert_not_contains \\\"cat $PWD/connect2.log\\\" \\\"experimental\\\"\\ne2e/cli/test_dotfiles_sync_files_encrypted:5:export MISE_EXPERIMENTAL=0\\nare readable only with a recipient's identity; the machine name, checkpoint\\nid and time, and the number of checkpoints stay visible (`machines` lists\\nthem without a key). Recipients default to this machine's own identities:\\nthe age key at `settings.age.key_file` (default `~/.config/mise/age.txt`)\\nand the public keys of `~/.ssh/id_ed25519` and `~/.ssh/id_rsa`. When none\\nexists, mise generates an age identity at the key file path (mode 0600)\\nand prints its public key. `--recipient <age1…|ssh-…|path>` (repeatable)\\nnames others: an age public key, an SSH public key, or a `.pub` or age\\nidentity file. The choice is recorded machine-locally as\\n`encrypt_backups = true` and `recipients = […]` in `[history.origin]`. To\\nrestore another machine's encrypted backup here, its identity must be\\namong the recipients and present here (`MISE_AGE_KEY`,\\n`settings.age.identity_files`, `settings.age.key_file`, or the default\\n`age.txt` and SSH keys); the identity file itself is a credential store,\\nnever captured or shared, so copy it between machines yourself.\\nConnecting again with a different choice (plaintext to encrypted, other\\nrecipients, or back) atomically replaces this machine's refs on the repository\\nwith eligible checkpoints under the new scheme, so a repository\\nnever holds a mix by accident. Encryption on without any usable recipient\\nuploads nothing and says so in `status` and `mise doctor`; plain text is\\nnever a fallback. A mise older than this feature skips encrypted refs\\nrather than misreading them. Encrypted backups protect recovery copies;\\nencrypted shared files are configured separately with `encrypt = true`\\nand `[history.encryption].recipients`. The `[env]` age directives remain experimental.\\n\\n**What is synchronized.** The setup branch mirrors the global configuration\\ndirectory at its root (`config.toml`, `conf.d/`, `tasks/`, templates),\\npublishes `[dotfiles]` sources under `sources/dotfiles/…` (relative to\\n`dotfiles.root`, resolved through the other machine's root) and\\n`sources/home/…`, and holds the shared version of every tracked entry under\\n`tracked/home/…` (a variant stream under `tracked/home@<variant>/…`). A\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"62b057\",\"wall_time_seconds\":5.001277042,\"session_id\":81612,\"original_token_count\":536,\"output\":\"   Compiling rustls-webpki v0.103.15\\n   Compiling sigstore-crypto v0.11.0\\n   Compiling sigstore-merkle v0.11.0\\n   Compiling tokio-rustls v0.26.4\\n   Compiling rustls-platform-verifier v0.7.0\\n   Compiling hyper-rustls v0.27.9\\n   Compiling reqwest v0.13.4\\n   Compiling aws-smithy-http-client v1.4.0\\n   Compiling aws-smithy-runtime v1.14.0\\n   Compiling astral-reqwest-middleware v0.5.1\\n   Compiling aube-util v2.2.9\\n   Compiling xx v2.6.1\\n   Compiling sigstore-tuf v0.11.0\\n   Compiling sigstore-rekor v0.11.0\\n   Compiling sigstore-tsa v0.11.0\\n   Compiling gix-transport v0.59.1\\n   Compiling http-cache-semantics v3.0.0\\n   Compiling mise-cache-core v0.1.0 (/Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-encryption/mise/crates/mise-cache-core)\\n   Compiling gix-protocol v0.65.1\\n   Compiling aws-runtime v1.9.1\\n   Compiling sigstore-bundle v0.11.0\\n   Compiling aube-manifest v2.2.9\\n   Compiling sigstore-trust-root v0.11.0\\n   Compiling aube-store v2.2.9\\n   Compiling rattler_redaction v0.2.3\\n   Compiling ambient-id v0.0.11\\n   Compiling astral_async_http_range_reader v0.11.0\\n   Compiling rattler_conda_types v0.51.0\\n   Compiling rattler_networking v0.30.6\\n   Compiling sigstore-verify v0.11.0\\n   Compiling gix v0.87.1\\n   Compiling aws-sdk-sso v1.108.0\\n   Compiling aws-sdk-ssooidc v1.110.0\\n   Compiling aws-sdk-sts v1.113.0\\n   Compiling aws-sdk-s3 v1.144.0\\n   Compiling mise-sigstore v0.1.0 (/Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-encryption/mise/crates/mise-sigstore)\\n   Compiling packslip v0.3.1\\n   Compiling aube-lockfile v2.2.9\\n   Compiling aube-registry v2.2.12\\n   Compiling aube-workspace v2.2.9\\n   Compiling aube-runtime v2.2.9\\n   Compiling aube-scripts v2.2.9\\n   Compiling aws-config v1.11.0\\n   Compiling aube-linker v2.2.9\\n   Compiling rattler_package_streaming v0.27.2\\n   Compiling rattler_shell v0.27.15\\n   Compiling rattler_solve v9.0.3\\n   Compiling rattler_virtual_packages v5.1.0\\n   Compiling rattler_menuinst v0.2.75\\n   Compiling rattler_cache v0.10.7\\n   Compiling rattler_repodata_gateway v0.33.0\\n   Compiling rattler v0.48.4\\nmbx[warning]: prediction was not restored: absolute path has no stable cache mapping: /opt/homebrew/opt/openssl@3/lib\\n\"}"}],"intern