{"timestamp":"2026-09-06T22:17:03.708Z","ordinal":9696,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a078cb-e5dc-7ea3-8898-6ef46eedfd49","call_id":"call_8DVTzMA4SsrVZuhidel3igrD","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 1.5 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"edaaee\",\"wall_time_seconds\":1.252893125,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":1836,\"output\":\"From https://github.com/jdx/mise\\n * branch                codex/dotfiles-launch-readiness -> FETCH_HEAD\\nPreparing worktree (new branch 'codex/dotfiles-onboarding-checks')\\nHEAD is now at 1e901234b feat(dotfiles): clarify sharing choices and private tracking\\n{\\\"comments\\\":{\\\"nodes\\\":[{\\\"body\\\":\\\"\\\\u003ca href=\\\\\\\"#\\\\\\\"\\\\u003e\\\\u003cimg alt=\\\\\\\"P1\\\\\\\" src=\\\\\\\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p1.svg?v=9\\\\\\\" align=\\\\\\\"top\\\\\\\"\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e **Private paths misreported remotely**\\\\n\\\\nA tracked `.local.toml` path keeps the default `backup = true`, but the backup builder excludes it because its coverage mode is `private`. This preview checks only the backup and encryption policies, so it lists the path under “Remote backup” as plaintext even though it will not be uploaded. This makes the connection disclosure and backup count inaccurate.\\\\n\\\\n\\\\u003ca href=\\\\\\\"https://app.greptile.com/ide/claude-code?prompt=This%20is%20a%20comment%20left%20during%20a%20code%20review.%0APath%3A%20src%2Fsystem%2Fhistory%2Fsync%2Forigin.rs%0ALine%3A%20287-288%0A%0AComment%3A%0A**Private%20paths%20misreported%20remotely**%0A%0AA%20tracked%20%60.local.toml%60%20path%20keeps%20the%20default%20%60backup%20%3D%20true%60%2C%20but%20the%20backup%20builder%20excludes%20it%20because%20its%20coverage%20mode%20is%20%60private%60.%20This%20preview%20checks%20only%20the%20backup%20and%20encryption%20policies%2C%20so%20it%20lists%20the%20path%20under%20%E2%80%9CRemote%20backup%E2%80%9D%20as%20plaintext%20even%20though%20it%20will%20not%20be%20uploaded.%20This%20makes%20the%20connection%20disclosure%20and%20backup%20count%20inaccurate.%0A%0A---%0A%0AFor%20each%20issue%20above%2C%20determine%20whether%20it%20is%20valid%20and%20should%20be%20fixed.%20If%20so%2C%20fix%20it%20directly.\\\\u0026repo=jdx%2Fmise\\\\u0026pr=12903\\\\u0026platform=github\\\\\\\"\\\\u003e\\\\u003cpicture\\\\u003e\\\\u003csource media=\\\\\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\\\\\" srcset=\\\\\\\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/FixInClaudeDark.svg?v=6\\\\\\\"\\\\u003e\\\\u003csource media=\\\\\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\\\\\\\" srcset=\\\\\\\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/FixInClaude.svg?v=6\\\\\\\"\\\\u003e\\\\u003cimg alt=\\\\\\\"Fix in Claude Code\\\\\\\" src=\\\\\\\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/FixInClaude.svg?v=6\\\\\\\"\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/picture\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\",\\\"databaseId\\\":3945434686}]},\\\"id\\\":\\\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fvdGE\\\",\\\"isResolved\\\":false}\\n{\\\"comments\\\":{\\\"nodes\\\":[{\\\"body\\\":\\\"\\\\u003ca href=\\\\\\\"#\\\\\\\"\\\\u003e\\\\u003cimg alt=\\\\\\\"P2\\\\\\\" src=\\\\\\\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p2.svg?v=9\\\\\\\" align=\\\\\\\"top\\\\\\\"\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e **Retracking shows wrong guidance**\\\\n\\\\nThis branch checks whether `--no-autosave` was supplied rather than the resulting policy. If an existing entry already has `autosave = false` and is retracked without repeating that flag, the setting remains disabled but the command reports watcher health instead of explaining that manual saves are still required. It may even recommend enabling a watcher that cannot save this path.\\\\n\\\\n\\\\u003ca href=\\\\\\\"https://app.greptile.com/ide/claude-code?prompt=This%20is%20a%20comment%20left%20during%20a%20code%20review.%0APath%3A%20src%2Fcli%2Fdotfiles%2Ftrack.rs%0ALine%3A%20149-155%0A%0AComment%3A%0A**Retracking%20shows%20wrong%20guidance**%0A%0AThis%20branch%20checks%20whether%20%60--no-autosave%60%20was%20supplied%20rather%20than%20the%20resulting%20policy.%20If%20an%20existing%20entry%20already%20has%20%60autosave%20%3D%20false%60%20and%20is%20retracked%20without%20repeating%20that%20flag%2C%20the%20setting%20remains%20disabled%20but%20the%20command%20reports%20watcher%20health%20instead%20of%20explaining%20that%20manual%20saves%20are%20still%20required.%20It%20may%20even%20recommend%20enabling%20a%20watcher%20that%20cannot%20save%20this%20path.%0A%0A---%0A%0AFor%20each%20issue%20above%2C%20determine%20whether%20it%20is%20valid%20and%20should%20be%20fixed.%20If%20so%2C%20fix%20it%20directly.\\\\u0026repo=jdx%2Fmise\\\\u0026pr=12903\\\\u0026platform=github\\\\\\\"\\\\u003e\\\\u003cpicture\\\\u003e\\\\u003csource media=\\\\\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\\\\\" srcset=\\\\\\\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/FixInClaudeDark.svg?v=6\\\\\\\"\\\\u003e\\\\u003csource media=\\\\\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\\\\\\\" srcset=\\\\\\\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/FixInClaude.svg?v=6\\\\\\\"\\\\u003e\\\\u003cimg alt=\\\\\\\"Fix in Claude Code\\\\\\\" src=\\\\\\\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/FixInClaude.svg?v=6\\\\\\\"\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/picture\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\",\\\"databaseId\\\":3945434689}]},\\\"id\\\":\\\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fvdGG\\\",\\\"isResolved\\\":false}\\n{\\\"comments\\\":{\\\"nodes\\\":[{\\\"body\\\":\\\"### Private retrack duplicates OS variants\\\\n\\\\n**Medium Severity**\\\\n\\\\n\\\\u003c!-- DESCRIPTION START --\\\\u003e\\\\n`--private` writes `share = false` onto existing variants, but a later `track --os`/`--profile` still treats variants as new when `share` differs. `contains` then appends a second matching variant, which `select` reports as ambiguous and drops from the tracked set, so the file is no longer protected.\\\\n\\\\u003c!-- DESCRIPTION END --\\\\u003e\\\\n\\\\n\\\\u003c!-- BUGBOT_BUG_ID: c9007a6b-6a17-42d2-821f-6d261ff49ed9 --\\\\u003e\\\\n\\\\n\\\\u003c!-- LOCATIONS START\\\\nsrc/cli/dotfiles/track.rs#L190-L205\\\\nLOCATIONS END --\\\\u003e\\\\n\\\\u003cdiv\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\\\\"https://cursor.com/open?REDACTED\\\\\\\" target=\\\\\\\"_blank\\\\\\\" rel=\\\\\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\\\\\"\\\\u003e\\\\u003cpicture\\\\u003e\\\\u003csource media=\\\\\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\\\\\" srcset=\\\\\\\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-cursor-dark.png\\\\\\\"\\\\u003e\\\\u003csource media=\\\\\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\\\\\\\" srcset=\\\\\\\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-cursor-light.png\\\\\\\"\\\\u003e\\\\u003cimg alt=\\\\\\\"Fix in Cursor\\\\\\\" width=\\\\\\\"115\\\\\\\" height=\\\\\\\"28\\\\\\\" src=\\\\\\\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-cursor-dark.png\\\\\\\"\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/picture\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u0026nbsp;\\\\u003ca href=\\\\\\\"https://cursor.com/agents?REDACTED\\\\\\\" target=\\\\\\\"_blank\\\\\\\" rel=\\\\\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\\\\\"\\\\u003e\\\\u003cpicture\\\\u003e\\\\u003csource media=\\\\\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\\\\\" srcset=\\\\\\\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-web-dark.png\\\\\\\"\\\\u003e\\\\u003csource media=\\\\\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\\\\\\\" srcset=\\\\\\\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-web-light.png\\\\\\\"\\\\u003e\\\\u003cimg alt=\\\\\\\"Fix in Web\\\\\\\" width=\\\\\\\"99\\\\\\\" height=\\\\\\\"28\\\\\\\" src=\\\\\\\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-web-dark.png\\\\\\\"\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/picture\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/div\\\\u003e\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n\\\\u003csup\\\\u003eReviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 1e901234b6ab920dd11bc0279eebf414b679cb05. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).\\\\u003c/sup\\\\u003e\\\\n\\\",\\\"databaseId\\\":3945435719}]},\\\"id\\\":\\\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fvdQr\\\",\\\"isResolved\\\":false}\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"519740\",\"wall_time_seconds\":2.91e-7,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":119,\"output\":\"  cargo-check –     Finished `dev` profile [unoptimized + debuginfo] target(s) in 4m 26s\\n  cargo-check – mbx[cache]: 1233 hits, 81 misses, 52 not looked up, 31 bypassed; 0 B downloaded, 0 B uploaded, 93.2 MiB stored locally\\n  cargo-check – mbx[savings]: 1233 compilations in, zero compiled. 6m 16s returned to circulation.\\n✔ cargo-check\\n  cargo-fmt – 603 files – **/*.rs – cargo fmt --all\\n❯ cargo-fmt – 4 files modified\\n✔ cargo-fmt – 4 files modified\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"c9ddc9\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000001208,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":371,\"output\":\"mbx[warning]: prediction was not restored: absolute path has no stable cache mapping: /opt/homebrew/opt/openssl@3/lib\\nmbx[warning]: result was not stored: rustc search path kind is not cacheable yet: native\\n    Finished `test` profile [unoptimized + debuginfo] target(s) in 1m 33s\\n     Running unittests src/main.rs (target/debug/deps/mise-86e301dc5f2a2a5a)\\n\\nrunning 13 tests\\ntest agecrypt::directive::tests::test_age_x25519_round_trip_large ... ok\\ntest agecrypt::directive::tests::test_age_x25519_round_trip_small ... ok\\ntest agecrypt::limits_tests::bounded_reader_accepts_limit_and_refuses_next_byte ... ok\\ntest agecrypt::plugin_tests::plugin_protocol_roundtrip_and_software_recovery ... ok\\ntest agecrypt::tests::test_classify_unsupported_ssh_identities ... ok\\ntest agecrypt::tests::test_decrypt_bytes_reports_the_wrong_identity ... ok\\ntest agecrypt::tests::test_encrypt_bytes_needs_a_recipient ... ok\\ntest agecrypt::tests::test_encrypt_bytes_round_trips_and_compresses ... ok\\ntest agecrypt::tests::test_generate_identity_file_is_private_and_never_overwrites ... ok\\ntest agecrypt::tests::test_parse_recipient ... ok\\ntest agecrypt::tests::test_resolve_recipient_arg_accepts_keys_and_f