{"timestamp":"2026-09-06T22:29:15.959Z","ordinal":10013,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a07177-9855-71a2-89cd-4a9a37cdbfcb","turn_id":"01a078ac-bf7f-7050-adcc-4d223220149d","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-d5562842-d728-4ae1-be1a-8ed291d0c5ca","process_id":"20759","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","gh pr view 12903 --repo jdx/mise --json body"],"cwd":"file:///Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-onboarding/mise","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"gh pr view 12903 --repo jdx/mise --json body"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"{\"body\":\"Connecting dotfile history should make it clear which files leave the machine and whether incoming edits will be written automatically. Interactive `origin set` now asks that separately from connection confirmation, while `--sync` selects a mode directly and `--yes` accepts the configured mode for existing automation.\\n\\nThe connection preview lists actual captured paths under local-only, shared-setup, and remote-backup destinations with encryption status. `track --private` disables both sharing and backups, including explicit variant sharing overrides; retracking preserves encryption. Watcher/manual-save guidance and the experimental tracking documentation are clarified.\\n\\nStacked on #12895 (`bootstrap/11-encrypted-backups`). File declarations can still be shared, and changing a policy does not erase previous uploads.\\n\\nValidation: new onboarding/privacy E2E and existing tracking, manual/automatic sync, encrypted backup/file, and sync-preflight E2E passed. Build, generated CLI documentation, scoped safe hk checks, and strict workspace Clippy (`--workspace --all-features --all-targets -- -D warnings`) passed on the completed stack.\\n\\n*AI-assisted — Tool: Codex; model: openai/unavailable; version: unavailable.*\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Changes default interactive origin connection (sync mode prompt) and what file contents leave the machine via `--private` and richer previews; automation using `origin set --yes` without `--sync` still auto-selects sync.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Improves dotfile **sharing and backup transparency** when connecting an origin and when tracking sensitive paths.\\n> \\n> **`track --private`** turns off both shared setup publication and remote recovery backups while keeping local history; variant `share` overrides are forced off, and retracking preserves existing encryption. Manual-save paths get clearer log lines; autosave health messaging is skipped when every tracked path is manual-only.\\n> \\n> **`origin set`** no longer silently defaults `--sync` to `sync` in interactive use: omitting `--sync` prompts whether to auto-publish and apply incoming changes (`no` → `manual`). **`--yes`** (or global yes) keeps the prior behavior by accepting the configured default without that prompt—scripts should pass **`--sync` explicitly**. The pre-connect disclosure now buckets current captured files into **Local only**, **Shared setup**, and **Remote backup** with plaintext/encryption labels, and backup counting excludes paths that are backup-only vs shared-only correctly.\\n> \\n> Docs and generated CLI help reflect the new flag, sync prompting, and revised experimental warnings; macOS CI runs a new **`test_dotfiles_onboarding`** E2E covering private vs shared vs backup-only tracking and manual sync mode.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 531b9bfc5a2f1b1df3c17bd76c05e21347676b0e. Bugbot is set up for automated code reviews on this repo. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\"}\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"{\"body\":\"Connecting dotfile history should make it clear which files leave the machine and whether incoming edits will be written automatically. Interactive `origin set` now asks that separately from connection confirmation, while `--sync` selects a mode directly and `--yes` accepts the configured mode for existing automation.\\n\\nThe connection preview lists actual captured paths under local-only, shared-setup, and remote-backup destinations with encryption status. `track --private` disables both sharing and backups, including explicit variant sharing overrides; retracking preserves encryption. Watcher/manual-save guidance and the experimental tracking documentation are clarified.\\n\\nStacked on #12895 (`bootstrap/11-encrypted-backups`). File declarations can still be shared, and changing a policy does not erase previous uploads.\\n\\nValidation: new onboarding/privacy E2E and existing tracking, manual/automatic sync, encrypted backup/file, and sync-preflight E2E passed. Build, generated CLI documentation, scoped safe hk checks, and strict workspace Clippy (`--workspace --all-features --all-targets -- -D warnings`) passed on the completed stack.\\n\\n*AI-assisted — Tool: Codex; model: openai/unavailable; version: unavailable.*\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Changes default interactive origin connection (sync mode prompt) and what file contents leave the machine via `--private` and richer previews; automation using `origin set --yes` without `--sync` still auto-selects sync.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Improves dotfile **sharing and backup transparency** when connecting an origin and when tracking sensitive paths.\\n> \\n> **`track --private`** turns off both shared setup publication and remote recovery backups while keeping local history; variant `share` overrides are forced off, and retracking preserves existing encryption. Manual-save paths get clearer log lines; autosave health messaging is skipped when every tracked path is manual-only.\\n> \\n> **`origin set`** no longer silently defaults `--sync` to `sync` in interactive use: omitting `--sync` prompts whether to auto-publish and apply incoming changes (`no` → `manual`). **`--yes`** (or global yes) keeps the prior behavior by accepting the configured default without that prompt—scripts should pass **`--sync` explicitly**. The pre-connect disclosure now buckets current captured files into **Local only**, **Shared setup**, and **Remote backup** with plaintext/encryption labels, and backup counting excludes paths that are backup-only vs shared-only correctly.\\n> \\n> Docs and generated CLI help reflect the new flag, sync prompting, and revised experimental warnings; macOS CI runs a new **`test_dotfiles_onboarding`** E2E covering private vs shared vs backup-only tracking and manual sync mode.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 531b9bfc5a2f1b1df3c17bd76c05e21347676b0e. Bugbot is set up for automated code reviews on this repo. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\"}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":242867333},"formatted_output":"{\"body\":\"Connecting dotfile history should make it clear which files leave the machine and whether incoming edits will be written automatically. Interactive `origin set` now asks that separately from connection confirmation, while `--sync` selects a mode directly and `--yes` accepts the configured mode for existing automation.\\n\\nThe connection preview lists actual captured paths under local-only, shared-setup, and remote-backup destinations with encryption status. `track --private` disables both sharing and backups, including explicit variant sharing overrides; retracking preserves encryption. Watcher/manual-save guidance and the experimental tracking documentation are clarified.\\n\\nStacked on #12895 (`bootstrap/11-encrypted-backups`). File declarations can still be shared, and changing a policy does not erase previous uploads.\\n\\nValidation: new onboarding/privacy E2E and existing tracking, manual/automatic sync, encrypted backup/file, and sync-preflight E2E passed. Build, generated CLI documentation, scoped safe hk checks, and strict workspace Clippy (`--workspace --all-features --all-targets -- -D warnings`) passed on the completed stack.\\n\\n*AI-assisted — Tool: Codex; model: openai/unavailable; version: unavailable.*\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Changes default interactive origin connection (sync mode prompt) and what file contents leave the machine via `--private` and richer previews; automation using `origin set --yes` without `--sync` still auto-selects sync.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> Improves dotfile **sharing and backup transparency** when connecting an origin and when tracking sensitive paths.\\n> \\n> **`track --private`** turns off both shared setup publication and remote recovery backups while keeping local history; variant `share` overrides are forced off, and retracking preserves existing encryption. Manual-save paths get clearer log lines; autosave health messaging is skipped when every tracked path is manual-only.\\n> \\n> **`origin set`** no longer silently defaults `--sync` to `sync` in interactive use: omitting `--sync` prompts whether to auto-publish and apply incoming changes (`no` → `manual`). **`--yes`** (or global yes) keeps the prior behavior by accepting the configured default without that prompt—scripts should pass **`--sync` explicitly**. The pre-connect disclosure now buckets current captured files into **Local only**, **Shared setup**, and **Remote backup** with plaintext/encryption labels, and backup counting excludes paths that are backup-only vs shared-only correctly.\\n> \\n> Docs and generated CLI help reflect the new flag, sync prompting, and revised experimental warnings; macOS CI runs a new **`test_dotfiles_onboarding`** E2E covering private vs shared vs backup-only tracking and manual sync mode.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 531b9bfc5a2f1b1df3c17bd76c05e21347676b0e. Bugbot is set up for automated code reviews on this repo. Configure [here](https: