{"timestamp":"2026-09-06T22:31:16.407Z","ordinal":10051,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a078d8-e8b7-7113-9d20-481cd89b76fc","call_id":"call_iZg8c8NlZ2Eg67931s507NXc","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.6 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"0407d8\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000003709,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":364,\"output\":\"version = 1\\nid = \\\"settle-dotfiles-pr-stack\\\"\\nkind = \\\"heartbeat\\\"\\nname = \\\"Settle dotfiles PR stack\\\"\\nprompt = \\\"Continue settling jdx/mise PRs #12849, #12835, #12838, #12843, #12865, #12882, #12895 (encryption), and #12903 (sharing choices and private tracking). The encryption agent has finished; include its completed work and follow-up in review, CI, integration, and restacking checks. Use isolated worktrees and preserve local changes. Read the latest handoff in /Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-takeover/TAKEOVER.md. Check new review feedback, substantive failing CI logs, and merge conflicts. Validate findings, fix valid issues in their earliest owning PR, restack safely with expected-head checks, reply with verification evidence and resolve only addressed or invalid findings. Preserve experimental tracking gates and released backward compatibility without compatibility scaffolding for unreleased stack revisions. Preserve the encryption implementation and never silently substitute plaintext. Never merge. Stop on unexpected remote pushes or required product clarification and request direction. Stay quiet when unchanged; notify only on actionable changes, blockers, or when all eight PRs are verified and ready for review. Pause this automation once the stack is settled.\\\"\\nstatus = \\\"ACTIVE\\\"\\nrrule = \\\"FREQ=MINUTELY;INTERVAL=30\\\"\\ntarget_thread_id = \\\"01a07177-9855-71a2-89cd-4a9a37cdbfcb\\\"\\ncreated_at = 1788710231122\\nupdated_at = 1788733171362\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"pr\":12904,\"chunk_id\":\"2cf4dc\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.275511208,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":436,\"output\":\"{\\\"body\\\":\\\"External updates and agent commands can edit tracked files without leaving a reliable before/after boundary. `mise bootstrap dotfiles capture --label \\\\\\\"omarchy update\\\\\\\" -- omarchy-update` now records a linked checkpoint pair and the command's outcome while preserving its exit status. Capture failures warn without preventing the external command from running.\\\\n\\\\n`history diff --operation [ref]` compares that operation with its recorded protective checkpoint rather than whichever save happens to precede it; without a reference it finds the newest operation even after later saves. `history --label` filters labeled checkpoints. No-op runs, failures, and crash recovery retain their labels and file state, including manual-save files.\\\\n\\\\nStacked on #12903 (`codex/dotfiles-launch-readiness`). Capture observes tracked files over an interval, including concurrent edits; it does not journal external writes individually or reverse package/service effects. Restore selected files from the recorded before checkpoint. Arbitrary command execution is explicitly unclassified in the command-effects catalog.\\\\n\\\\nValidation: capture and existing bootstrap-history E2E passed, including exit 37, signal exit 143, spawn failure, disabled history, no-op capture, later saves, and SIGKILL recovery. All 66 history unit tests and 5 command-effects tests passed. Build, CLI/man generation, scoped safe hk checks, and strict workspace Clippy (`--workspace --all-features --all-targets -- -D warnings`) passed. Added macOS CI coverage; Linux discovers the test automatically.\\\\n\\\\n*AI-assisted — Tool: Codex; model: openai/unavailable; version: unavailable.*\\\\n\\\",\\\"headRefOid\\\":\\\"a71e43940353081e9272ee2ce068b75d3cbc94c2\\\",\\\"mergeable\\\":\\\"CONFLICTING\\\"}\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"pr\":12905,\"