erified and ready for review. Pause this automation once the complete stack is settled.\"}));\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(\"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-takeover/TAKEOVER.md\\n@@\\n # Dotfiles stack takeover\\n+\\n+## Scope correction: entire TEN-PR stack\\n+\\n+User explicitly requested the entire stack, including two more PRs. Live open-PR branch-chain inventory confirms #12904 feat(dotfiles): capture history around external commands (base codex/dotfiles-launch-readiness, head codex/dotfiles-command-capture, expected remote a71e43940353081e9272ee2ce068b75d3cbc94c2), then #12905 test(dotfiles): exercise recovery across three machines (base codex/dotfiles-command-capture, head codex/dotfiles-recovery-acceptance, expected remote c627ea6233fba82722e031c4e3ceda97f833319d). #12904 currently CONFLICTING against the updated #12903; #12905 currently MERGEABLE against its old base. Neither new branch has been edited or restacked by this task yet. Prioritize integration/restack/testing both in isolated worktrees with exact-head leases. The earlier eight-head local verification does NOT verify these two layers.\\n+\\n+Existing heartbeat updated to cover ALL TEN, plus rediscover the full open base/head chain on each pass to avoid missing additional descendants. Existing eight current heads and CI run IDs below remain unchanged. No new automation created. Do not declare settled until capture, three-machine recovery acceptance, review feedback, and CI on both new heads are included. No merges.\\n*** End Patch\"));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a078d8-8fe1-7512-8383-08263a40e40e","create_time":1788733876.967979}}}
