{"timestamp":"2026-09-06T22:32:54.914Z","ordinal":10093,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a078da-6982-78f1-a02b-febe5c6617c0","call_id":"call_2HeRyl4lBGp23Nv4KRHSV10A","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 1.6 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"3a2d9a\",\"wall_time_seconds\":1.001147333,\"session_id\":9796,\"original_token_count\":247,\"output\":\"[detached HEAD 823ba5c24] feat(dotfiles): capture history around external commands\\n 16 files changed, 384 insertions(+), 36 deletions(-)\\n create mode 100644 docs/cli/bootstrap/dotfiles/capture.md\\n create mode 100644 e2e/cli/test_dotfiles_capture\\n create mode 100644 src/cli/dotfiles/capture.rs\\nSuccessfully rebased and updated refs/heads/codex/dotfiles-capture-checks.\\nmise WARN  GitHub OAuth refresh was rejected (incorrect_client_credentials): The client_id and/or client_secret passed are incorrect.. Reauthorization is required; run `mise token github --oauth --refresh`\\nmise WARN  GitHub OAuth refresh was rejected (incorrect_client_credentials): The client_id and/or client_secret passed are incorrect.. Reauthorization is required; run `mise token github --oauth --refresh`\\nmise WARN  GitHub OAuth refresh was rejected (incorrect_client_credentials): The client_id and/or client_secret passed are incorrect.. Reauthorization is required; run `mise token github --oauth --refresh`\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"dcbc36\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.246522375,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":2579,\"output\":\"{\\\"comments\\\":{\\\"nodes\\\":[{\\\"body\\\":\\\"\\\\u003ca href=\\\\\\\"#\\\\\\\"\\\\u003e\\\\u003cimg alt=\\\\\\\"P1\\\\\\\" src=\\\\\\\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p1.svg?v=9\\\\\\\" align=\\\\\\\"top\\\\\\\"\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e **Tracked paths lose after-state**\\\\n\\\\nAfter the external command returns, `refresh_tracked()` replaces the tracked set from the start of the operation with the current configuration. The following `prepare_capture()` therefore promotes only the refreshed set. If the command removes a tracked entry while also editing that file, the before checkpoint includes the file but the outcome does not read its live contents. The linked checkpoints then fail to preserve the file's actual after-state. Preserve both the start-time and end-time tracked entries during outcome capture, and cover this case with a test.\\\\n\\\\n\\\\u003ca href=\\\\\\\"https://app.greptile.com/ide/claude-code?prompt=This%20is%20a%20comment%20left%20during%20a%20code%20review.%0APath%3A%20src%2Fcli%2Fdotfiles%2Fcapture.rs%0ALine%3A%2057-58%0A%0AComment%3A%0A**Tracked%20paths%20lose%20after-state**%0A%0AAfter%20the%20external%20command%20returns%2C%20%60refresh_tracked%28%29%60%20replaces%20the%20tracked%20set%20from%20the%20start%20of%20the%20operation%20with%20the%20current%20configuration.%20The%20following%20%60prepare_capture%28%29%60%20therefore%20promotes%20only%20the%20refreshed%20set.%20If%20the%20command%20removes%20a%20tracked%20entry%20while%20also%20editing%20that%20file%2C%20the%20before%20checkpoint%20includes%20the%20file%20but%20the%20outcome%20does%20not%20read%20its%20live%20contents.%20The%20linked%20checkpoints%20then%20fail%20to%20preserve%20the%20file's%20actual%20after-state.%20Preserve%20both%20the%20start-time%20and%20end-time%20tracked%20entries%20during%20outcome%20capture%2C%20and%20cover%20this%20case%20with%20a%20test.%0A%0A---%0A%0AFor%20each%20issue%20above%2C%20determine%20whether%20it%20is%20valid%20and%20should%20be%20fixed.%20If%20so%2C%20fix%20it%20directly.\\\\u0026repo=jdx%2Fmise\\\\u0026pr=12904\\\\u0026platform=github\\\\\\\"\\\\u003e\\\\u003cpicture\\\\u003e\\\\u003csource media=\\\\\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\\\\\" srcset=\\\\\\\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/FixInClaudeDark.svg?v=6\\\\\\\"\\\\u003e\\\\u003csource media=\\\\\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\\\\\\\" srcset=\\\\\\\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/FixInClaude.svg?v=6\\\\\\\"\\\\u003e\\\\u003cimg alt=\\\\\\\"Fix in Claude Code\\\\\\\" src=\\\\\\\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/FixInClaude.svg?v=6\\\\\\\"\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/picture\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\",\\\"databaseId\\\":3945444490}]},\\\"id\\\":\\\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fveta\\\",\\\"isResolved\\\":false}\\n{\\\"comments\\\":{\\\"nodes\\\":[{\\\"body\\\":\\\"\\\\u003ca href=\\\\\\\"#\\\\\\\"\\\\u003e\\\\u003cimg alt=\\\\\\\"P2\\\\\\\" src=\\\\\\\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p2.svg?v=9\\\\\\\" align=\\\\\\\"top\\\\\\\"\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e **Identity setup comes too late**\\\\n\\\\nThe recovery instructions run both rollback commands before telling the user to configure the recovery identity. Resolving `laptop/latest` decrypts the checkpoint even during `--dry-run`, so these steps fail on a fresh machine without an identity. Move the identity setup before the rollback commands and name a supported configuration method.\\\\n\\\\n\\\\u003ca href=\\\\\\\"https://app.greptile.com/ide/claude-code?prompt=This%20is%20a%20comment%20left%20during%20a%20code%20review.%0APath%3A%20docs%2Fhistory.md%0ALine%3A%20526%0A%0AComment%3A%0A**Identity%20setup%20comes%20too%20late**%0A%0AThe%20recovery%20instructions%20run%20both%20rollback%20commands%20before%20telling%20the%20user%20to%20configure%20the%20recovery%20identity.%20Resolving%20%60laptop%2Flatest%60%20decrypts%20the%20checkpoint%20even%20during%20%60--dry-run%60%2C%20so%20these%20steps%20fail%20on%20a%20fresh%20machine%20without%20an%20identity.%20Move%20the%20identity%20setup%20before%20the%20rollback%20commands%20and%20name%20a%20supported%20configuration%20method.%0A%0A---%0A%0AFor%20each%20issue%20above%2C%20determine%20whether%20it%20is%20valid%20and%20should%20be%20fixed.%20If%20so%2C%20fix%20it%20directly.\\\\u0026repo=jdx%2Fmise\\\\u0026pr=12905\\\\u0026platform=github\\\\\\\"\\\\u003e\\\\u003cpicture\\\\u003e\\\\u003csource media=\\\\\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\\\\\" srcset=\\\\\\\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/FixInClaudeDark.svg?v=6\\\\\\\"\\\\u003e\\\\u003csource media=\\\\\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\\\\\\\" srcset=\\\\\\\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/FixInClaude.svg?v=6\\\\\\\"\\\\u003e\\\\u003cimg alt=\\\\\\\"Fix in Claude Code\\\\\\\" src=\\\\\\\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/FixInClaude.svg?v=6\\\\\\\"\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/picture\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\",\\\"databaseId\\\":3945445185}]},\\\"id\\\":\\\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fve1P\\\",\\\"isResolved\\\":false}\\n{\\\"comments\\\":{\\\"nodes\\\":[{\\\"body\\\":\\\"\\\\u003ca href=\\\\\\\"#\\\\\\\"\\\\u003e\\\\u003cimg alt=\\\\\\\"P2\\\\\\\" src=\\\\\\\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p2.svg?v=9\\\\\\\" align=\\\\\\\"top\\\\\\\"\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e **Assertion misses earlier leaks**\\\\n\\\\nThis checks only whether the recovery-only file exists at the current `main` tip, so it does not prove that the file never appeared on the shared branch. A regression that publishes the file and removes it during a later sync would still pass. Check all commits reachable from `main`, or assert after each publication point.\\\\n\\\\n**Knowledge Base Used:** [Testing and end-to-end validation](https://app.greptile.com/jdx-org/-/custom-context/knowledge-base/jdx/mise/-/docs/testing-and-end-to-end-validation.md)\\\\n\\\\nNote: If this suggestion doesn't match your team's coding style, reply to this and let me know. I'll remember it for next time!\\\\n\\\\n\\\\u003ca href=\\\\\\\"https://app.greptile.com/ide/claude-code?prompt=This%20is%20a%20comment%20left%20during%20a%20code%20review.%0APath%3A%20e2e%2Fcli%2Ftest_dotfiles_recovery_journey%0ALine%3A%20103%0A%0AComment%3A%0A**Assertion%20misses%20earlier%20leaks**%0A%0AThis%20checks%20only%20whether%20the%20recovery-only%20file%20exists%20at%20the%20current%20%60main%60%20tip%2C%20so%20it%20does%20not%20prove%20that%20the%20file%20never%20appeared%20on%20the%20shared%20branch.%20A%20regression%20that%20publishes%20the%20file%20and%20removes%20it%20during%20a%20later%20sync%20would%20still%20pass.%20Check%20all%20commits%20reachable%20from%20%60main%60%2C%20or%20assert%20after%20each%20publication%20point.%0A%0A**Knowledge%20Base%20Used%3A**%20%5BTesting%20and%20end-to-end%20validation%5D%28https%3A%2F%2Fapp.greptile.com%2Fjdx-org%2F-%2Fcustom-context%2Fknowledge-base%2Fjdx%2Fmise%2F-%2Fdocs%2Ftesting-and-end-to-end-validation.md%29%0A%0A---%0A%0AFor%20each%20issue%20above%2C%20determine%20whether%20it%20is%20valid%20and%20should%20be%20fixed.%20If%20so%2C%20fix%20it%20directly.\\\\u0026repo=jdx%2Fmise\\\\u0026pr=12905\\\\u0026platform=github\\\\\\\"\\\\u003e\\\\u003cpicture\\\\u003e\\\\u003csource media=\\\\\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\\\\\" srcset=\\\\\\\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/FixInClaudeDark.svg?v=6\\\\\\\"\\\\u003e\\\\u003csource media=\\\\\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\\\\\\\" srcset=\\\\\\\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/FixInClaude.svg?v=6\\\\\\\"\\\\u003e\\\\u003cimg alt=\\\\\\\"Fix in Claude Code\\\\\\\" src=\\\\\\\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/FixInClaude.svg?v=6\\\\\\\"\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/picture\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\",\\\"databaseId\\\":3945445186}]},\\\"id\\\":\\\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fve1Q\\\",\\\"isResolved\\\":false}\\n{\\\"comments\\\":{\\\"nodes\\\":[{\\\"body\\\":\\\"_🔒 Security \\\\u0026 Privacy_ | _🟠 Major_ | _⚡ Quick win_\\\\n\\\\n\\\\u003cdetails\\\\u003e\\\\n\\\\u003csummary\\\\u003e🧩 Analysis chain\\\\u003c/summary\\\\u003e\\\\n\\\\n🏁 Script executed:\\\\n\\\\n```shell\\\\nsed -n '1,125p' e2e/cli/test_dotfiles_recovery_journey\\\\nprintf '\\\\\\\\n--- assert_fail definition/usages ---\\\\\\\\n'\\\\nrg -n '(^|[[:space:]])assert_fail([[:space:]]|\\\