rc/system/history/sync/preflight.rs\"},{\"body\":\"### This-machine refs use backups\\n\\n**Medium Severity**\\n\\n\\u003c!-- DESCRIPTION START --\\u003e\\n`machines` lists this host from local checkpoints, but `rollback --to \\u003cthis-name\\u003e/\\u003cref\\u003e` resolves only fetched `refs/machines/` backups. \",\"comment\":3945289138,\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fvFtn\",\"path\":\"src/system/history/sync/machines.rs\"},{\"body\":\"_🔒 Security \\u0026 Privacy_ | _🟠 Major_ | _⚡ Quick win_\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003e🧩 Analysis chain\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n🏁 Script executed:\\n\\n```shell\\n#!/bin/bash\\n# Resolve where the shared config file lives and whether it is inside the publis\",\"comment\":3945310329,\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fvJLV\",\"path\":\"src/system/history/sync/origin.rs\"},{\"body\":\"_🗄️ Data Integrity \\u0026 Integration_ | _🟡 Minor_ | _⚡ Quick win_\\n\\n**Take the sync lock before you rewrite `sync.json`.**\\n\\n`bootstrap_completed` performs a read-modify-write of the whole `SyncStatus` file without holding the\",\"comment\":3945310331,\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fvJLX\",\"path\":\"src/system/history/sync/run.rs\"}],\"pr\":\"p12865\"}\n{\"open\":[{\"body\":\"_🎯 Functional Correctness_ | _🟠 Major_ | _⚡ Quick win_\\n\\n**Remove the stale origin-local sync override.** `Settings::get()` loads `settings.history.sync` from `config.local.toml`, while `mise settings set history.sync ...\",\"comment\":3944697691,\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6ftl4k\",\"path\":\"src/system/history/sync/origin.rs\"},{\"body\":\"_🎯 Functional Correctness_ | _🟠 Major_ | _🏗️ Heavy lift_\\n\\n**Keep the normal bootstrap preview in the target-side dry-run path.**\\n\\nWhen the target has history synchronization enabled, `run_from()` returns immediately afte\",\"comment\":3944932227,\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fuMZC\",\"path\":\"src/cli/bootstrap.rs\"},{\"body\":\"\\u003ca href=\\\"#\\\"\\u003e\\u003cimg alt=\\\"P2\\\" src=\\\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p2.svg?v=9\\\" align=\\\"top\\\"\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003e **Origin Removal Fails Immediately**\\n\\nIf the watcher or an explicit sync or pull currently holds the sync\",\"comment\":3945468513,\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fvir5\",\"path\":\"src/system/history/sync/origin.rs\"},{\"body\":\"### Onboard blocks bootstrap on any pause\\n\\n**Medium Severity**\\n\\n\\u003c!-- DESCRIPTION START --\\u003e\\n`configuration_held` becomes true whenever incoming configuration is still pending or any configuration path is conflicted. A who\",\"comment\":3945469818,\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fvi6K\",\"path\":\"src/system/history/sync/onboard.rs\"},{\"body\":\"### Conflict count doubled after onboard\\n\\n**Low Severity**\\n\\n\\u003c!-- DESCRIPTION START --\\u003e\\n`undecided` adds `applied.held` to `synced.conflicts`. On a conflicted setup, apply already reports `held` as the conflict count, so \",\"comment\":3945469819,\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fvi6L\",\"path\":\"src/system/history/sync/onboard.rs\"},{\"body\":\"### Setup repos clone when store fails\\n\\n**Medium Severity**\\n\\n\\u003c!-- DESCRIPTION START --\\u003e\\nIf the history store is unavailable, `from_git` logs a debug line and returns `None`, so a marked setup repository is cloned into th\",\"comment\":3945469822,\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fvi6O\",\"path\":\"src/system/history/sync/onboard.rs\"},{\"body\":\"The opening makes a broad recommendation and promises “one command” before explaining the prerequisites. Lead with what the reader will do; leave comparisons and implementation details to the reference pages.\\n\\nReplace th\",\"comment\":3945471047,\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fvjHl\",\"path\":\"docs/bootstrap/setup.md\"},{\"body\":\"Start with local tracking, without requiring a GitHub account. The current example also mixes a macOS shell file with a Linux desktop directory, and never says where to put the service declaration. Use one existing file \",\"comment\":3945471049,\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fvjHn\",\"path\":\"docs/bootstrap/setup.md\"},{\"body\":\"Move these sections immediately before connecting a repository: readers should try recovery before publishing anything. Remove invented timestamps and checkpoint IDs. Also qualify rollback publication: a connected reposi\",\"comment\":3945471053,\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fvjHq\",\"path\":\"docs/bootstrap/setup.md\"},{\"body\":\"The transcript repeats the following paragraph and is likely to drift as prompts change. Replace both with explicit mode selection and a short decision table. Keep the backup disclosure: excluding a file from sharing doe\",\"comment\":3945471055,\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fvjHs\",\"path\":\"docs/bootstrap/setup.md\"},{\"body\":\"Introduce the second machine before discussing two-machine conflicts. The fresh-machine snippet currently omits PATH setup and installing gh; even `mise use -g gh` does not activate its executable in an otherwise unconfi\",\"comment\":3945471057,\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fvjHu\",\"path\":\"docs/bootstrap/setup.md\"},{\"body\":\"The current example says the result differs per machine but puts the email in shared configuration, so both machines get the same value. It also omits the actual template. Make this a complete optional example without pr\",\"comment\":3945471062,\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fvjHy\",\"path\":\"docs/bootstrap/setup.md\"},{\"body\":\"The platform list mixes onboarding, package management, service internals, and compatibility notes. Keep this guide focused on selecting files and checking tracking. Do not encourage tracking entire desktop trees before \",\"comment\":3945471065,\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fvjH0\",\"path\":\"docs/bootstrap/setup.md\"}],\"pr\":\"p12882\"}\n{\"open\":[{\"body\":\"\\u003ca href=\\\"#\\\"\\u003e\\u003cimg alt=\\\"P1\\\" src=\\\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p1.svg?v=9\\\" align=\\\"top\\\"\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003e **Background sync starts plugins**\\n\\nDuring unattended publication, the `interactive` flag controls decryp\",\"comment\":3945467630,\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fviid\",\"path\":\"src/system/history/sync/files.rs\"}],\"pr\":\"p12895\"}\n{\"open\":[{\"body\":\"_🔒 Security \\u0026 Privacy_ | _🟠 Major_ | _⚡ Quick win_\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003e🧩 Analysis chain\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n🏁 Script executed:\\n\\n```shell\\n#!/bin/bash\\nset -e\\nprintf '%s\\\\n' '--- track option and policy construction ---'\\nsed -n '40,7\",\"comment\":3945441550,\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fveO2\",\"path\":\"src/cli/dotfiles/track.rs\"},{\"body\":\"### Piped yes no longer connects origin\\n\\n**Medium Severity**\\n\\n\\u003c!-- DESCRIPTION START --\\u003e\\nThe new mode question reads stdin whenever `--sync` is omitted, so a piped confirmation is consumed before `Connect this setup repo\",\"comment\":3945470675,\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fvjDj\",\"path\":\"src/cli/dotfiles/origin.rs\"}],\"pr\":\"p12903\"}\n{\"open\":[{\"body\":\"\\u003ca href=\\\"#\\\"\\u003e\\u003cimg alt=\\\"P1\\\" src=\\\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p1.svg?v=9\\\" align=\\\"top\\\"\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003e **Tracked paths lose after-state**\\n\\nAfter the external command returns, `refresh_tracked()` replaces the \",\"comment\":3945444490,\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fveta\",\"path\":\"src/cli/dotfiles/capture.rs\"}],\"pr\":\"p12904\"}\n{\"open\":[{\"body\":\"\\u003ca href=\\\"#\\\"\\u003e\\u003cimg alt=\\\"P2\\\" src=\\\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p2.svg?v=9\\\" align=\\\"top\\\"\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003e **Identity setup comes too late**\\n\\nThe recovery instructions run both rollback commands before telling th\",\"comment\":3945445185,\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fve1P\",\"path\":\"docs/history.md\"},{\"body\":\"\\u003ca href=\\\"#\\\"\\u003e\\u003cimg alt=\\\"P2\\\" src=\\\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p2.svg?v=9\\\" align=\\\"top\\\"\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003e **Assertion misses earlier leaks**\\n\\nThis checks only whether the recovery-only file exists at the current\",\"comment\":3945445186,\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fve1Q\",\"path\":\"e2e/cli/test_dotfiles_recovery_journey\"},{\"body\":\"_🔒 Security \\u0026 Privacy_ | _🟠 Major_ | _⚡ Quick win_\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003e🧩 Analysis chain\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n🏁 Script executed:\\n\\n```shell\\nsed -n '1,125p' e2e/cli/test_dotfiles_recovery_journey\\nprintf '\\\\n--- assert_fail definition/\",\"comment\":3945462246,\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fvhpA\",\"path\":\"e2e/cli/test_dotfiles_recovery_journey\"}],\"pr\":\"p12905\"}\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"{\"open\":[],\"pr\":\"p12835\"}\n{\"open\":[],\"pr\":\"p12838\"}\n{\"open\":[{\"body\":\"### Appeared pending tree skips capture\\n\\n**Medium Severity**\\n\\n\\u003c!-- DESCRIPTION START --\\u003e\\nWhen a pending tracked path appears, the watcher replans and installs new watches but reconciles only if an existing anchor inode w\",\"comment\":3945467924,\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fvilu\",\"path\":\"src/system/history/watch/runtime.rs\"}],\"pr\":\"p12843\"}\n{\"open\":[],\"pr\":\"p12849\"}\n{\"open\":[{\"body\":\"_🎯 Functional Correctness_ | _🟡 Minor_ | _⚡ Quick win_\\n\\n**Record the start of the current sync-failure streak.** When `sync()` fails before any fetch or publish succeeds, it persists `last_error` but no failure timestamp\",\"comment\":3944671871,\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fthu_\",\"path\":\"src/cli/doctor/mod.rs\"},{\"body\":\"_🔒 Security \\u0026 Privacy_ | _🟡 Minor_ | _⚡ Quick win_\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003e🧩 Analysis chain\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n🏁 Script executed:\\n\\n```shell\\n#!/bin/bash\\n# Confirm the repository's convention for a platform null path.\\nrg -n -C 3 '\\\"NUL\",\"comment\":3944671879,\"id\":\"PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fthvD\",\"path\":\"src/git.rs\"},{\"body\":\"### Checkpoint re-upload can brick sync\\n\\n**High Severity**\\n\\n\\u003c!-- DESCRIPTION START --\\u003e\\nUploading a checkpoint that already exists on t