`age1tag` public\nsettings.toml:32:[age.identity_files]\nsettings.toml:41:default_docs = \"~/.config/mise/age.txt\"\nsettings.toml:47:[age.ssh_identity_files]\nsettings.toml:2968:default_docs = \"~/.config/mise/age.txt\"\n","exit_code":2,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":4708},"formatted_output":"rg: src/age.rs: No such file or directory (os error 2)\ndocs/history.md:371:the age key at `settings.age.key_file` (default `~/.config/mise/age.txt`)\ndocs/history.md:380:`settings.age.identity_files`, `settings.age.key_file`, or the default\ndocs/history.md:381:`age.txt` and SSH keys); the identity file itself is a credential store,\ndocs/history.md:579:(`github_tokens.toml`, `age.txt`, `*.key`, …) are neither shared nor backed\ndocs/history.md:660:local identity file with `settings.age.identity_files`. Native `age1tag` public\nsettings.toml:32:[age.identity_files]\nsettings.toml:41:default_docs = \"~/.config/mise/age.txt\"\nsettings.toml:47:[age.ssh_identity_files]\nsettings.toml:2968:default_docs = \"~/.config/mise/age.txt\"\n"},"started_at_ms":1788734511057,"completed_at_ms":1788734511057}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-06T22:41:51.138Z","ordinal":10282,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a07177-9855-71a2-89cd-4a9a37cdbfcb","turn_id":"01a078d9-c0cd-7843-901a-b76dfa554ca0","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-87d6e440-93ac-4eb8-a6dd-ba54179cb704","process_id":"62688","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","head -65 /Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-takeover/TAKEOVER.md"],"cwd":"file:///Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/141d/mise","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"head -65 /Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-takeover/TAKEOVER.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"# Dotfiles stack takeover\n\n## Scope correction: entire TEN-PR stack\n\nUser explicitly requested the entire stack, including two more PRs. Live open-PR branch-chain inventory confirms #12904 feat(dotfiles): capture history around external commands (base codex/dotfiles-launch-readiness, head codex/dotfiles-command-capture, expected remote a71e43940353081e9272ee2ce068b75d3cbc94c2), then #12905 test(dotfiles): exercise recovery across three machines (base codex/dotfiles-command-capture, head codex/dotfiles-recovery-acceptance, expected remote c627ea6233fba82722e031c4e3ceda97f833319d). #12904 currently CONFLICTING against the updated #12903; #12905 currently MERGEABLE against its old base. Neither new branch has been edited or restacked by this task yet. Prioritize integration/restack/testing both in isolated worktrees with exact-head leases. The earlier eight-head local verification does NOT verify these two layers.\n\nExisting heartbeat updated to cover ALL TEN, plus rediscover the full open base/head chain on each pass to avoid missing additional descendants. Existing eight current heads and CI run IDs below remain unchanged. No new automation created. Do not declare settled until capture, three-machine recovery acceptance, review feedback, and CI on both new heads are included. No merges.\n\n## Latest completed push: eight-PR stack including encryption and onboarding\n\nAtomic exact-lease push60945 SUCCEEDED, no unexpected remote changes. All eight PRs verified MERGEABLE and non-draft after push. Expected remote heads now:\n- #12849 bootstrap/5-track = 3f967b8809e2d12163c31e0237adabc299532b68\n- #12835 bootstrap/6-rollback = 19b1756b5d7bdf16b0e7310f170111a46ae43de6\n- #12838 bootstrap/7-user-services = 384a89a2fdb45a970f653550f43a9e8450a76340\n- #12843 bootstrap/8-watch = 7e0e5584b36ee6bfaa3bd65b37399e64c29497b1\n- #12865 bootstrap/9-origin = 996764d5f2fd87e95278395570c69d2fac2418b5\n- #12882 bootstrap/10-auto-sync = 4281da00d537de7fd9751ed7133277f5acbead39\n- #12895 bootstrap/11-encrypted-backups = 7ec3e38b7e9fbc2aac38d70f8a925b0d439d8a40\n- #12903 codex/dotfiles-launch-readiness = 531b9bfc5a2f1b1df3c17bd76c05e21347676b0e\n\nLocal worktrees/branches as below, all clean after commits. No tool sessions remain running. Top render/lint/E2Es session36666 PASS; duplicate parallel E2E16107 also PASS. E2Es onboarding, track, full two-machine sync cover all three #12903 fixes and prior core contract. Encryption full verification recorded below. Original141d and other agentf730 untouched. No merges; blog unchanged here.\n\nExplicit test.yml CI dispatched and headSha verified for all eight: #12849=34064079053; #12835=34064078985; #12838=34064078972; #12843=34064079030; #12865=34064079123; #12882=34064078971; #12895=34064079051; #12903=34064079038. Last snapshot builds/windows/macOS running or queued, no substantive failure yet. Must inspect these runs, not stale original-head CI. Updated #12895/#12903 descriptions with current integration evidence and pending CI links. Real Secure Enclave/TPM hardware remains untested.\n\nPosted evidence replies for seven findings: 3945285524 -> r3945462752; 3945310321 -> r3945462751; 3945310318 -> r3945462754; 3945294364 -> r3945462749; 3945434686 -> r3945462757; 3945434689 -> r3945462748; 3945435719 -> r3945462760. Resolved the four still open; three had already been resolved by bots after push. Do not repost. Older unresolved origin/auto review queue below remains and fresh reviews may arrive. #12895 had no unresolved findings when inspected. Git-for-Windows hooksPath finding not dismissed: upstream docs recommend /dev/null and wrappers special-case exact path, but appended hook-name behavior still needs platform verification; do not assert invalid based only on fopen mapping.\n\nHeartbeat settle-dotfiles-pr-stack ACTIVE every30min and now explicitly includes ALL EIGHT. Keep checking feedback/failing checks/merge conflicts until settled. Preserve completed encryption, no plaintext fallback. Stop unexpected pushes. This stack is not yet declared settled or CI-verified.\n\n## Latest update: encryption added to checks (September 6)\n\nUPDATE: Scope is EIGHT PRs, not seven. Found finished-agent follow-up #12903 above encryption, branch codex/dotfiles-launch-readiness expected remote head1e901234b6ab920dd11bc0279eebf414b679cb05. Heartbeat updated again to include it. New isolated worktree /Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-onboarding/mise branch codex/dotfiles-onboarding-checks. Rebased its one commit onto encryption7ec3e38b7; current head7f74d0922 plus uncommitted fixes for all three reviews: private backup preview excludes walk.private (3945434686/PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fvdGE), retrack guidance follows resulting autosave policy (3945434689/PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fvdGG), selector equality ignores share to avoid duplicate private OS variants (3945435719/PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fvdQr). Added onboarding E2E regressions and experimental opt-in, deduplicated experimental docs. Session36666 RUNNING full render then lint-fix then onboarding/track/sync E2Es. No push yet, no replies yet.\n\nEncryption verification COMPLETE/PASS: build81612, full render+lint78487, 39 sync unit tests9393, 13 age tests75066, E2E41886 encrypted backups, encrypted files, encryption schema, sync_permissions/purge, sync_preflight (281s). Integration committed7ec3e38b7e9fbc2aac38d70f8a925b0d439d8a40. Encryption worktree clean. All older sessions complete. Next wait36666, fix failures, commit top, verify remote eight heads then atomic exact-lease push and dispatch test.yml for EACH updated head. Reply/resolve four core and three top findings with evidence, report pending CI accurately. Real hardware remains untested.\n\nUser explicitly included the finished encryption PR. The seven-PR scope now includes #12895, branch bootstrap/11-encrypted-backups, expected remote head11147666527317c2cfcb389f261a64922548976c. Its original full dispatched CI34059651602 passed and no unresolved threads were present. Existing heartbeat settle-dotfiles-pr-stack updated to include encryption (no duplicate automation). Preserve implementation, no plaintext fallback, no merges.\n\nCore final session57064 PASSED: render, lint-fix, sync_permissions, sync_preflight, rollback_review, bootstrap_from_git. All six local branches clean at the heads below; still NOT PUSHED. Encryption isolated worktree /Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-encryption/mise, branch codex/dotfiles-encryption-checks, rebased all five commits after old base d7a800310874a115ea813a851ea7c9b9d344206c onto auto4281da00d. Rebase COMPLETE, head0d658e3a7 plus uncommitted integration fixes. Other agent worktreef730 untouched. Build session81612 running.\n\nEncryption integration fixes: preserve Result-returning read_status and lock/update_status APIs, combine doctor backup health with failure-streak health, retain backup dedup regression tests in upload_tests module (encryption tests stay tests), accept encrypt in strict incoming declaration whitelist, keep normal uploads non-forced (scheme/policy changes use encryption's dedicated replace transaction), adapt fixtures to CoverageEntry.encrypt and new upload arguments. Encryption E2Es updated to opt into experimental tracking while env-age gate assertion explicitly disables experimental. Need compile, focused units/E2Es incl encrypted and core permission/preflight, render/lint, commit, then exact-lease push all seven and dispatch CI each head. Generated mise.usage.kdl chose ours during conflicts and MUST render. No replies/resolutions this heartbeat yet; four addressed core review IDs below still need replies after push.\n\n## IN PROGRESS heartbeat September 6 21:43 UTC: main rebase and three new fixes\n\nUPDATE: full local restack completed; no push yet. Local heads now foundation3f967b8809e2d12163c31e0237adabc299532b68, rollback19b1756b5d7bdf16b0e7310f170111a46ae43de6, services384a89a2fdb45a970f653550f43a9e8450a76340, watcher7e0e5584b36ee6bfaa3bd65b37399e64c29497b1, origin996764d5f2fd87e95278395570c69d2fac2418b5, auto4281da00d537de7fd9751ed7133277f5acbead39. All clean at start of final render. Full render/lint passed foundation through origin, with generated docs commits on each owning branch. Only RUNNING session57064: top full render, then lint-fix, then E2Es sync_permissions (purge), sync_preflight, rollback_review, bootstrap_from_git. Poll it before commits/push. All older sessions below complete.\n\nFourth new fix: #9 rejects unknown top-level keys in incoming whole-file declarations (only incoming validation; released local parser unchanged). Prevents shrae=false silently becoming share=true. New sync_preflight regression PASSED (51405); owning rebased code commit9b5ba2b5e, original4c911682d. Needs reply/resolve3945310318 PRRT_kwDOIvux3s6fvJLQ after push. Variant fix nowbbecdbe4c; rollback fix5399cb731; purge fix4281da00d. Other three new findings need replies after push as below. Still no GitHub replies this heartbeat.\n\nNo pushes or GitHub replies yet in this heartbeat. Expected remote heads are the six in the completed push below (a04a62048/dbb901d75/3edad6aa8/3b00de37e/7a9037390/5cb5808). Verified unchanged at start. Main advanced to b396c62bc (CLI reference rewrite #12885); foundation conflicted and prevented normal PR test workflows, only review/title checks ran on prior push. Never claim last pushed heads passed full CI.\n\nFoundation rebased onto b396c62bc and committed regenerated docs in 3f967b880. Preserved new main bootstrap help, merged dotfile status help, and kept new cli-reference.ts generator/tests in tasks.toml alongside optional-subcommand normalization. Generated-file conflicts selected ours and were fully regenerated afterwards. Foundation full render/lint-fix + track_experimental E2E PASS; clean.\nRollback rebased onto foundation, new head19b1756b5 (includes regenerated reference). New fix originally aec7d03a2, now5399cb731: optional directory cleanup treats unreadable-descendant inspection as reason to preserve directory, not abort whole rollback. Regression adds chmod000 child and verifies neighbor deletion + child preservation. E2E54105 PASS; rebased full render/lint32515 PASS; clean.\nServices rebased onto rollback, headbd9e4196e before generated docs commit. Resolved source bootstrap help: retain new concise phase order, add user services and post-tool service phase; retain cross-platform services help. Full render/lint session22217 RUNNING. Must poll, review generated diff, commit, then restack watcher.\nWatcher still OLD current3b00de37e, not yet rebased; rebase onto services using old base3edad6aa8, resolve docs, render/lint/commit.\nOrigin still based on old watcher; own new commit5508f8073 rejects empty variant names and `/`/`@` separators. New cross-platform variant round-trip unit PASS (14914), lint-fix PASS. Rebase onto new watcher using old base3b00de37e after ready, render/lint.\nAuto still based on old origin; own new commit3d148c7b4 reuses held purge lock for disconnect and acquires lock before standalone remove rewrites config. New helper remove_locked uses run::SyncStatus. Added purge regression to test_dotfiles_sync_permissions: delete this-machine recovery refs, disconnected status, shared main remains. Initial lint44102 failed wrong type module, fixed; final lint+E2E7957 PASS. Rebase onto new origin using old base7a9037390 when ready, 