{"timestamp":"2026-09-06T22:42:09.505Z","ordinal":10285,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_02be90ffdd5dff4a016a9dec31c9b087d0a2ff7887b64d9bb8","status":"completed","call_id":"call_dfWNse5DPus3giNR3im3sqL2","name":"exec","input":"text(await tools.apply_patch(\"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-recovery/mise/docs/history.md\\n@@\\n-After bootstrapping a spare machine from your setup repository, fetch the latest\\n-recovery refs and inspect a machine-specific file that was backed up but not shared:\\n+After bootstrapping a spare machine from your setup repository, configure its\\n+recovery identity locally using `settings.age.identity_files`, or place the key\\n+in `~/.config/mise/age.txt` with permissions `0600`. Do this before either rollback\\n+command below: the dry run also needs to decrypt the backup. Then fetch the latest\\n+recovery refs and inspect a machine-specific file that was backed up but not shared:\\n@@\\n-Configure the recovery identity locally before restoring. Verify the recovered\\n-file and its permissions; `mise bootstrap dotfiles undo` reverses the restore.\\n+Verify the recovered file and its permissions;\\n+`mise bootstrap dotfiles undo` reverses the restore.\\n*** Update File: /Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-recovery/mise/e2e/cli/test_dotfiles_recovery_journey\\n@@\\n require_cmd git\\n+export MISE_EXPERIMENTAL=1\\n@@\\n-assert_fail \\\"git --git-dir=$origin cat-file -e main:tracked/home/.config/journey/monitor\\\"\\n+shared_commits=$(git --git-dir=\\\"$origin\\\" rev-list main)\\n+assert_succeed 'test -n \\\"$shared_commits\\\"'\\n+for shared_commit in $shared_commits; do\\n+  assert_fail \\\"git --git-dir=$origin cat-file -e $shared_commit:tracked/home/.config/journey/monitor\\\"\\n+done\\n*** End Patch\"));\ntext(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"RUSTUP_TOOLCHAIN=1.95.0 mise run render && RUSTUP_TOOLCHAIN=1.95.0 mise run lint-fix && RUSTUP_TOOLCHAIN=1.95.0 mise run test:e2e '^test_dotfiles_recovery_journey$'\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-recovery/mise\",\"yield_time_ms\":1000,\"max_output_tokens\":1500}));\ntext(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"gh api repos/jdx/mise/pulls/comments/3945467924 --jq .body\",\"max_output_tokens\":4000}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a078d9-c0cd-7843-901a-b76dfa554ca0","create_time":1788734511.883936}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-06T22:42:09.519Z","ordinal":10286,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a07177-9855-71a2-89cd-4a9a37cdbfcb","turn_id":"01a078d9-c0cd-7843-901a-b76dfa554ca0","item":{"type":"FileChange","id":"exec-f54cccfe-9824-457e-b3ef-67f55a292aa7","changes":{"/Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-recovery/mise/docs/history.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -529,3 +529,6 @@\n \n-After bootstrapping a spare machine from your setup repository, fetch the latest\n+After bootstrapping a spare machine from your setup repository, configure its\n+recovery identity locally using `settings.age.identity_files`, or place the key\n+in `~/.config/mise/age.txt` with permissions `0600`. Do this before either rollback\n+command below: the dry run also needs to decrypt the backup. Then fetch the latest\n recovery refs and inspect a machine-specific file that was backed up but not shared:\n@@ -539,4 +542,4 @@\n \n-Configure the recovery identity locally before restoring. Verify the recovered\n-file and its permissions; `mise bootstrap dotfiles undo` reverses the restore.\n+Verify the recovered file and its permissions;\n+`mise bootstrap dotfiles undo` reverses the restore.\n Try this while the original machine is still available. Successful publication\n","move_path":null},"/Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/dotfiles-recovery/mise/e2e/cli/test_dotfiles_recovery_journey":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -5,2 +5,3 @@\n require_cmd git\n+export MISE_EXPERIMENTAL=1\n \n@@ -102,2 +103,6 @@\n # The recovery-only file never appeared on the shared setup branch.\n-assert_fail \"git --git-dir=$origin cat-file -e main:tracked/home/.config/journey/monitor\"\n+shared_commits=$(git --git-dir=\"$origin\" rev-list main)\n+assert_succeed 'test -n \"$shared_commits\"'\n+for shared_commit in $shared_commits; do\n+  assert_fail \"git --git-dir=$origin cat-file -e $shared_commit:tracked/home/.config/journey/monitor\"\n+done\n","move_path":null}},"status":"completed",