{"timestamp":"2026-09-06T22:42:11.149Z","ordinal":10288,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a07177-9855-71a2-89cd-4a9a37cdbfcb","turn_id":"01a078d9-c0cd-7843-901a-b76dfa554ca0","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-3a23761d-c45c-4820-90cf-882926cb8451","process_id":"35698","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","gh api repos/jdx/mise/pulls/comments/3945467924 --jq .body"],"cwd":"file:///Users/jdx/.codex/worktrees/141d/mise","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"gh api repos/jdx/mise/pulls/comments/3945467924 --jq .body"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"### Appeared pending tree skips capture\n\n**Medium Severity**\n\n<!-- DESCRIPTION START -->\nWhen a pending tracked path appears, the watcher replans and installs new watches but reconciles only if an existing anchor inode was replaced. A directory (or tree) that materializes already populated — mkdir, extract, or `mv` into place — produces no file-level events after the new watch is attached, so its contents stay unsaved until the next periodic reconcile, and stay unsaved indefinitely if `history.watch.reconcile` is `0`.\n<!-- DESCRIPTION END -->\n\n<!-- BUGBOT_BUG_ID: 9127bd05-79be-4105-acb0-8afccb951f4b -->\n\n<!-- LOCATIONS START\nsrc/system/history/watch/runtime.rs#L419-L466\nLOCATIONS END -->\n<div><a href=\"https://cursor.com/open?REDACTED\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-cursor-dark.png\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-cursor-light.png\"><img alt=\"Fix in Cursor\" width=\"115\" height=\"28\" src=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-cursor-dark.png\"></picture></a>&nbsp;<a href=\"https://cursor.com/agents?REDACTED\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-